// Accepting a step turns its run into the review of what landed: the changes take the conversation's place, with a
// commit box above them and the open steps to go on with under the step.

// decided: the move is the browser's own view transition on the Changes section; no transition, no animation
// decided: a commit takes only the step's files, its snapshot, and its spec when it isn't a draft, so other work stays out
// decided: Claude writes the message in a one-off headless run from the step and its diff, not in the step's chat
// decided: .claude/settings.local.json is your local permissions, so it's left out of Changes and the commit

